{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["The Urim and the Tummim — like the sworn declarations of the holy Name of 'the Holy One, blessed be He', which He would place in the breastplate to declare their judgment and their needs. If the nations tell them their oracles and their divinations by an unclean spirit, to distinguish — what countless distinctions — between impurity and purity: how much more so for holiness, which it declares!"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The phrase שבעות של שמות is translated as 'sworn declarations of the holy Name'; the syntax of להבדיל כמה הבדלות is rendered literally, as Rashbam's compressed style leaves the exact clause relationship somewhat open."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:29.231669314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}